<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.braatz.dated-gates — the calendar half of the State Machine, mechanical.
  Daily 09:30 local: ~/repos/ceo-desk/dated-gates.py run — fires date-gated cards (close-mode runs the
  gate script and bb-closes with the receipt; nudge-mode posts the at-bat on the card once).
  Born fable-smDrainDesk-03, 2026-09-05: seven of 81 frozen cards were "come back on date X".
  Repo-backed here per the S38 launchd-census rule. Heartbeat: ~/.local/state/dated-gates/heartbeat
  (register in ~/Scripts/darwin-heartbeats.py — teed to smDrainScripts3's wrap, darwin-scripts was claimed).

  NOT DARWIN'S ALONE (F27, ceo-desk 597c631/370d151, 2026-09-07): dated-gates.py takes an atomic day-lock on the HUB
  (n8n:/var/tmp/dated-gates/<date>.lock, `box` inside says who fired) before it fires anything. This agent is the
  09:30 CT first-chair; feynman's systemd user timer (ceo-desk/systemd/dated-gates.timer, 09:45 CT) is the
  understudy and fires only if darwin lost the lock to nobody. The journal is repo-backed (ceo-desk/state/fired.jsonl,
  pull-in/commit-out), so both boxes read one history. If darwin is asleep at 09:30, feynman fires; SUCCESS IS SILENT.
  Read the receipt, never fire by hand: `dated-gates.py list` + `ssh n8n cat /var/tmp/dated-gates/<date>.lock/box`.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.braatz.dated-gates</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/jasoncbraatz/repos/ceo-desk/dated-gates.py</string>
    <string>run</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <dict>
    <key>Hour</key><integer>9</integer>
    <key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer>
  </dict>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/Users/jasoncbraatz/Library/Logs/dated-gates.out</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/Users/jasoncbraatz/Library/Logs/dated-gates.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
